{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/277780-geist-as-a-minor-template","id":277780,"title":"Geist as a Minor Template?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Geist: The Sin-Eaters"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-10-10T19:59:45-07:00","id":277780,"title":"Geist as a Minor Template?","content":"<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rVC9b5ewDcQLjg-_EKytYZIvpqYIdZMCiRoynnxYAXE/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">So, I've been working on this thing...</a><br /> <br /> Basically, one thing that's struck me about Geist is that it boils down to &quot;you play the spooky ghost stories&quot;. And, well...<br /> <br /> I wanted something that would let me <i>investigate</i> the spooky ghost stories without trivializing them.<br /> <br /> Basically, I have all the stuff up to the actual template, character creation instructions, and template-unique merits written up; right now, I have the method you would take to get the template in play (as well as a quick rules-hack for 2e Geist).<br /> <br /> Some notes: <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>I will be keeping the &quot;come back to life over and over again&quot; aspect; after all, that's half the fun of Sin-Eater! However, it's going to be &quot;integrated&quot; into the <i>Reaper's Bargain</i> condition, which promises that you'll die the &quot;proper&quot; way within a year.</li> <li>A year, that is, unless you renegotiate. There will be a couple ways of putting off your death, from helping Ghosts pass on to getting <i>other</i> people to die the right way.</li> <li>You aren't inextricably bound to your Geist; basically, you can get access to your Template benefits as long as you have a Ghost Fettered to you. It's just that the <i>not dying like a punk</i> part of the template kinda needs someone who can handle the Bargain.</li> <li>Maybe some way to convert whichever Ghost you are hosting into a Geist, if you put the proper effort into it. This'll probably require Underworld runs and everything; I will probably jury-rig a simplified Underworld travel system that fits with the template.</li> <li>Because, well... I want people to be able to run these guys without any books other than 2e Core and the rules doc.</li> <li>They don't get splats or anything; I'm taking a more Hunter approach, where you pick up Initiation merits that get you some neat supernatural oomph.</li> </ol><br /> So, I'd appreciate any thoughts; you can leave your comments here or in the actual document.<br /> <br /> My expectations is there will be a lot of screaming and throwing things in my general direction; I am prepared to take the blows!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-11T07:09:34-07:00","id":278106,"title":"","content":"'Screams and throws things at you'<br /> <br /> Actually, I think you're going to get largely ignored in here. You're basically just converting Geists into the hunter version - like hunters have dread power versions of vampires if you don't want to completely stat out a vamp. Doesn't really apply to this forum: you might have better luck in the Hunter forum since you're largely throwing out the actual Geist rules.<br /> <br /> If you want to know how Geists ACTUALLY work, this might be a good place to ask.","signature":""